*.pth
*.npy
KnowAir.npy
# ...except data/altitude.npy: small (1.4MB), static, and required just to
# build the city graph (graph.py) - unlike KnowAir.npy it's not experiment
# output or ~300MB user-supplied data, so it's fine (and necessary) to ship.
!data/altitude.npy

# ...and data/SensorAir.npy: also small (4.3MB) and, unlike KnowAir.npy,
# built from a ~268MB raw source (data/data.csv, see
# data/prepare_sensor_dataset.py) that's too large to commit and isn't
# tracked here - shipping the small derived .npy directly (plus
# site_sensor.txt below) is what lets dataset_num 4 work on a fresh
# clone with no extra download, matching KnowAir/dataset 1-3's
# "just clone and run" experience despite data.csv being absent.
!data/SensorAir.npy

# data/data.csv: the ~268MB raw source above - regenerate SensorAir.npy/
# site_sensor.txt from it (data/prepare_sensor_dataset.py) only if you
# want a different window/site-coverage tradeoff than the committed one;
# not needed otherwise, and too large to commit itself.
data/data.csv

# Editor-specific settings (machine-local paths, not meant to be shared)
.vscode/

# Not part of this repo's own work - a large local results-archive
# download and a personal citation-manager file that both got swept into
# a commit once via an IDE "stage all" action. ref/ is a personal
# reference folder, not something this project publishes; the zip is a
# ~845MB download that GitHub's 100MB per-file limit would reject anyway.
/3-20260830T050539Z-1-001.zip
/ref/
